  "raw": ", which in part says:\n\nBeginning Jan. 1, 2012, a private kindergarten or preschool must be licensed by the State Board of Education to enroll five or more participants and no later than Oct. 1 year-round.\n\nThe bill has been assigned to the Committee on Public Affairs, where a public hearing will be held on Tuesday, April 27, 2010, at 9 a.m. Public testimony will be welcomed. No hearing record is available. I will be a witness at public hearings by requesting that a \"No\" vote be recorded on or after May 10, 2010, stating that it would be a public meeting at which I would be willing to comment on the issue. The hearing date is one of the rare days when there is no Assembly meeting.\n\nAs I often discuss on my blog, most California private kindergartens are private not for the sake of being private, but as a safety valve for parents of preschoolers with very limited options because of low enrollment.",
  "serialized": ", which in part says: Beginning Jan. 1, 2012, a private kindergarten or preschool must be licensed by the State Board of Education to enroll five or more participants and no later than Oct. 1 year-round. The bill has been assigned to the Committee on Public Affairs, where a public hearing will be held on Tuesday, April 27, 2010, at 9 a.m. Public testimony will be welcomed. No hearing record is available. I will be a witness at public hearings by requesting that a \"No\" vote be recorded on or after May 10, 2010, stating that it would be a public meeting at which I would be willing to comment on the issue. The hearing date is one of the rare days when there is no Assembly meeting. As I often discuss on my blog, most California private kindergartens are private not for the sake of being private, but as a safety valve for parents of preschoolers with very limited options because of low enrollment.",
